  "findings": [
    "The official Survey of India index lists 27 state/UT village-boundary archives. The latest acquisition downloaded and audited 10 of 27; 17 remain missing because some archives exceed the 50 MiB per-file limit or timed out/terminated.",
    "The latest run contains 21,952 features and 7 invalid geometries, including six in Punjab and one in Andaman and Nicobar Islands.",
    "Across two acquisition runs, 12 distinct jurisdiction archives have been recovered; Telangana's prior-run shapefile has a CRS metadata conflict between custom LCC_WGS84 PRJ and XML claiming EPSG:3857.",
    "These are village administrative boundaries, not Assembly Constituency polygons.",
    "Many features have null or repeated Vill_LGD codes. Repeated codes may represent multiple urban ward/feature fragments; do not deduplicate without geometry and identity rules.",
    "Census 2011 population linkage requires a validated village-code crosswalk and accepted AC geometry; no constituency population estimate is inferred from these files alone."
  ],
  "decision": "Use acquired files only as source-audited village administrative geometry candidates. Do not insert into the runtime or canonical AC geometry registry until full national coverage, per-file CRS, LGD identity, topology and effective-date checks pass.",
